# Copy to /etc/faas/sealed.env on the Droplet and fill in.
# This file is read by systemd EnvironmentFile= — one VAR=value per line.

# Postgres — default uses peer auth over Unix socket.
DATABASE_URL=postgres:///faas?host=/run/postgresql&user=faas

# Dev token for API testing (apid creates a dev account on first boot).
# Must match fp_live_<48-hex> format.
# This placeholder is substituted by `make bootstrap` with
# `openssl rand -hex 24` so no committed secret ever leaves the repo (issue #85, PR 2).
# The v2 path is `make bootstrap` + `gregale manifest {validate,render}` +
# `gregale release install`; the v1 bootstrap.sh path was retired by
# issue #911 / PR-1 on 2026-08-15.
FAAS_DEV_TOKEN=__DEV_TOKEN__

# Public OCI image ref for the builder base (issue #938, ADR-114).
# This must be replaced with the linux/amd64 digest produced by
# .github/workflows/images.yml before a named compute node is started.
# The imaged daemon fails closed when FAAS_NODE_NAME is set but this value
# is empty or tag-only; a mutable latest tag is never a production default.
# Resolve the platform-specific digest from the immutable full-SHA tag via:
#   crane digest ghcr.io/poyrazk/builder-base:sha-<full-git-sha> \
#     --platform linux/amd64
# imaged rejects manifest lists at cmd/imaged/main.go:392-401, so the
# pin must be the linux/amd64-specific digest (not the multi-arch tag).
#
# The alpine ref below is a placeholder that satisfies imaged's startup
# check but produces empty builder VMs (no /usr/local/bin/faas-guest-init,
# no railpack, no buildkit — see issue #938 Blocker 3). DO NOT run
# `gregale deploy` against this placeholder; the build will die on the
# first cold boot when vmmd's waitReady times out at 30s.
#
# Use mirror.gcr.io — Docker Hub's anonymous pull rate limit (100/6h per IP)
# throttles unauthenticated droplet IPs and turns imaged's startup check into
# an endless 429 crash loop (observed on the DO deploy, 2026-07-24).
# mirror.gcr.io serves the same content-addressed blobs with no auth and no
# rate limit; the pinned digest is portable across both registries.
FAAS_BUILDER_BASE_REF=__SET_TO_BUILDER_BASE_DIGEST__

# Runtime base refs (Tier 1 PR 2, ADR-052 + ADR-053). Named compute nodes
# MUST set every ref, including the generic minimal base, to a platform-specific
# immutable digest. An unset value is only accepted by an unnamed dev daemon;
# production fails closed instead of allowing a mutable `:latest` base to drift.
# The env var MUST be digest-pinned — a tag-only value fails imaged startup loud.
#
# FAAS_DEPLOY_BASE_REF_DEBIAN_PARENT=mirror.gcr.io/library/debian@sha256:...
# FAAS_DEPLOY_BASE_REF_MINIMAL=ghcr.io/poyrazk/base-minimal@sha256:...
# FAAS_DEPLOY_BASE_REF_NODE22=mirror.gcr.io/library/node@sha256:...
# FAAS_DEPLOY_BASE_REF_PYTHON312=mirror.gcr.io/library/python@sha256:...
# FAAS_DEPLOY_BASE_REF_GO124=mirror.gcr.io/library/golang@sha256:...
# FAAS_DEPLOY_BASE_REF_GO124_ALPINE=mirror.gcr.io/library/golang@sha256:...
# FAAS_DEPLOY_BASE_REF_NODE24=mirror.gcr.io/library/node@sha256:...
# FAAS_DEPLOY_BASE_REF_PYTHON313=mirror.gcr.io/library/python@sha256:...

# Apps domain — set by `make bootstrap` (v2 path; the v1 bootstrap.sh path was retired by issue #911 / PR-1 on 2026-08-15).
FAAS_APPS_DOMAIN=__DROPLET_IP__.nip.io

# Session key for dashboard cookies (32-byte hex).
# Generate: openssl rand -hex 32 > /etc/faas/secrets/session.key
# The key is NO LONGER written here — see the v2 path: `gregalectl secrets init` followed by `gregalectl backup unseal-archive-creds`. The v1 bootstrap.sh step (A4) was retired by issue #911 / PR-1 on 2026-08-15.
# apid picks it up via systemd LoadCredential= and Environment=
# (see deploy/digitalocean/systemd/faas-apid.service).

# GitHub App (set after creating the app in github.com/settings/apps).
# FAAS_GITHUB_APP_ID=
# FAAS_GITHUB_APP_KEY_PATH=/etc/faas/secrets/github-app.pem
# FAAS_GITHUB_WEBHOOK_SECRET=
# FAAS_GITHUB_APP_INSTALL_URL=https://github.com/apps/gregale-platform/installations/new
# The hosted default is the Gregale App above. Set this for a different
# GitHub App slug or a GitHub Enterprise App installation endpoint.
#
# PR-D / ADR-012 §7 amendment: per-tenant webhook secrets now
# override this platform fallback. The resolver at
# pkg/githubd/webhook_secret.go reads github_webhook_secrets by
# installation_id first; this env var is the fallback for
# installs that haven't been migrated. Use
# `gregale github-webhook-secret set --installation-id <id>
# --secret <hex>` to rotate per-tenant.

# Mega-PR-A (issue #911 / ADR-110 PR-1) — the multi-box identity
# every daemon reads at boot. The systemd drop-in (deploy/ansible/
# roles/<role>/templates/99-faas-node-name.conf.j2) is the canonical
# source; sealed.env is a fallback for containerised-deploys paths
# that don't carry the ansible drop-in. Single-box dev leaves this
# commented out (the daemons short-circuit to "legacy single-box"
# when the env is empty). Multi-box operators set
# FAAS_NODE_NAME=<host> to match host_vars/faas-fsn-N.yml.
# FAAS_NODE_NAME=__NODE_NAME__

# Polar is the public-release billing provider. It is also the code default
# when FAAS_BILLING_PROVIDER is omitted. The access token, webhook secret,
# product IDs, and meter ID below must belong to the same Polar environment.
# FAAS_POLAR_SANDBOX accepts "1" or "true"; empty = production. Env wins over
# [billing.polar] TOML (matching pkg/billing/loader/config.go's
# ApplyBillingEnvOverlay); use the TOML form for typed config in a
# container, the env form for the systemd EnvironmentFile= path.
# FAAS_BILLING_PROVIDER=polar
# FAAS_POLAR_ACCESS_TOKEN=polar_...
# FAAS_POLAR_WEBHOOK_SECRET=polar_whs_...
# FAAS_POLAR_HOBBY_PRODUCT_ID=prod_...
# FAAS_POLAR_PRO_PRODUCT_ID=prod_...
# FAAS_POLAR_SCALE_PRODUCT_ID=prod_...
# FAAS_POLAR_USAGE_EVENT_NAME=faas_ram_usage
# FAAS_POLAR_METER_ID=meter_...
# FAAS_POLAR_SANDBOX=1

# Sign-in OAuth (issue #419 / ADR-046). Both providers optional;
# apid boots cleanly when BOTH vars per provider are unset (the
# provider is treated as disabled and /v1/auth/<provider> returns
# 503 oauth_provider_unavailable). A half-set pair refuses to boot
# — set both, unset both, or don't start apid. The optional
# *_REDIRECT_URI overrides the host-derived default.
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=<oauth-client-id>.apps.googleusercontent.com
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=<oauth-client-secret>
# GOOGLE_REDIRECT_URI=https://<box>/v1/auth/google/callback
# GITHUB_CLIENT_ID=<oauth-app-client-id>
# GITHUB_CLIENT_SECRET=<oauth-app-client-secret>
# GITHUB_REDIRECT_URI=https://<box>/v1/auth/github/callback

# Stripe billing portal URL template (issue #142). Legacy Stripe
# opt-in only — if you've set FAAS_BILLING_PROVIDER=stripe on a node
# (NOT the default at v2), the changePlan 402 falls through to this
# template URL with `{account_id}` substituted to the caller's account
# ID. On a Polar-default node the 402 carries the provider-neutral
# `checkout_url` + `tx_id`; the loader never reads this var when the
# provider can create hosted checkout. Operator-controlled; a wrong value
# silently misroutes every blocked upgrade on a legacy Stripe node.
# FAAS_BILLING_PORTAL_URL=https://billing.example.com/portal?account={account_id}

# --- transactional email (ADR-115 / spec G4 closure) ---
# Resend is the production transactional-email provider (ADR-115 §D1).
# The Resend API key MUST be scoped to "Sending access" only in the
# Resend dashboard (ADR-115 §D4) — never "Full access". The From
# address must be on a verified domain whose SPF + DKIM records are
# published at the DNS provider (ADR-115 §D3); Resend rejects with
# HTTP 403 if the From domain is unverified.
#
# Contract: FAAS_MAIL_TRANSPORT selects the transport at daemon boot.
# Empty / unset / "log" → LogSender (safe for dev / CI / unit tests).
# "resend" / "postmark" → live transport; the matching credential
# env var MUST be set or apid + meterd refuse to boot
# (ADR-115 §D5 fail-closed contract). Unknown transport → WARN +
# LogSender fallback.
#
# Verified-domain requirement: Resend/Postmark dashboards surface the
# SPF/DKIM records; paste them at your DNS provider before flipping
# the transport on. DNS automation is a separate follow-on
# (ADR-115 §D.5 deferred).
#
# Sub-processors are pre-listed at docs/compliance/subprocessors.md
# (Resend + Postmark) and docs/DPA.md:150-155. No DPA amendment is
# required to switch between them.
#
# FAAS_MAIL_TRANSPORT=resend
# FAAS_MAIL_RESEND_API_KEY=re_...
# FAAS_MAIL_FROM=Gregale <noreply@your-verified-domain.example>
#
# Issue #246 acceptance item 8: Svix / Standard Webhooks signing
# secret Resend stamps on every bounce / complaint / delivery.
# Copy the value from Resend's dashboard → Webhooks → "Signing
# Secret". Empty fails closed — the apid /v1/webhooks/resend
# handler returns 503, so a missing env var cannot silently accept
# unsigned events. The secret rotates via "Roll" in the Resend
# dashboard; update the row here and restart apid.
# FAAS_MAIL_RESEND_WEBHOOK_SECRET=whsec_...
#
# Postmark fallback (ADR-115 §D2 — operator-selectable alternative
# to Resend via FAAS_MAIL_TRANSPORT=postmark). Set FAAS_MAIL_FROM to
# a Postmark-verified sender address; the same SPF/DKIM + key-scoping
# requirements apply.
# FAAS_MAIL_POSTMARK_TOKEN=<postmark-server-token>

# apid extras.
# Loopback-only bind: spec §11 says only gatewayd-public is reachable from outside.
# gatewayd-internal reverse-proxies /v1, /dashboard, /oauth, /login, /auth/verify,
# /logout, /status, /healthz onto this loopback listener.
FAAS_APID_LISTEN=127.0.0.1:8081
# FAAS_PROMETHEUS_URL=http://127.0.0.1:9095

# Host age key (gap G2 — sealed at rest, IAM-2 / issue #186 MFA):
#   * FAAS_HOST_AGE_RECIPIENT_PATH is the PUBLIC half (host.age.pub, mode 0444)
#     apid reads at startup so /v1/apps/{name}/secrets (PUT) can seal.
#   * FAAS_HOST_AGE_IDENTITY_PATH is the PRIVATE half (host.age, mode 0400 root:root);
#     apid consumes it via systemd LoadCredential (deploy/systemd/faas-apid.service),
#     so the env var here only matters when running apid outside systemd (e.g. local dev)
#     apid reads at startup so /v1/account/mfa/{verify,confirm,recover,disable}
#     can unseal TOTP secrets. NOT in sealed.env — delivered via systemd
#     LoadCredential= (see deploy/digitalocean/systemd/faas-apid.service) so
#     the other five control-plane daemons never see the private half.
# Both files are written by vmmd on first boot (pkg/secretbox/hostkey.go:97).
# FAAS_HOST_AGE_RECIPIENT_PATH=/etc/faas/secrets/host.age.pub

# Issue #250 — Hetzner Storage Box off-host backup wiring.
# The user half + host half of the SFTP credential. Both are surfaced
# to the rclone.conf template at ansible-run time; the rclone.conf
# itself is sealed-at-rest under /etc/faas/secrets/storage-box/
# (PR #371 cosign precedent — host.age) and decrypted into a tmpfs
# staging dir before systemd's LoadCredential= surfaces the plaintext
# to the postgresql + faas-pg-basebackup-push units.
#
# HETZNER_STORAGE_BOX_USER is the SFTP user (u123456.subdomain on
# Hetzner's Storage Box); HETZNER_STORAGE_BOX_HOST is the SSH-via-SFTP
# endpoint (u123456.your-storagebox.de).
#
# Both vars are REQUIRED — the postgres_backup role fails closed on
# missing values (deploy/ansible/roles/postgres_backup/tasks/main.yml
# fail-closed assert).
# HETZNER_STORAGE_BOX_USER=u123456
# HETZNER_STORAGE_BOX_HOST=u123456.your-storagebox.de
